{"authored" [{"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{2x}=-2x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}-2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+6{x}^{2}=4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4x-6{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(3-x)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)={x}^{2}(2-x)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)={x}^{2}(2x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5=6{x}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-5x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-5x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0e9557bc289a385db8bf9c44da5b79510320b94269dc606286c46432610d8eb4" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=3{x}^{4}-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-4{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+C \\\\ -1 & =-2(0)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1e5a8e0774d9ef906c9cb679cdb322103479a1ee249965dfdefc9c07c2eb1a9" "basis" 1154 "