/assets/cece096a5b267821994e9b6d8142f0d7ea684bbe8e28da7cdb01b87a73f1db4c.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "33d31df5c002d4c09c8da6a49f2643388148a2099bf31895c57ea2ce62f4fc26" "basis" 1203 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "33d31df5c002d4c09c8da6a49f2643388148a2099bf31895c57ea2ce62f4fc26" "basis" 1203 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(x-3)^{2}{y}^{′}=8$ that satisfies the condition $y(4)=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "33d31df5c002d4c09c8da6a49f2643388148a2099bf31895c57ea2ce62f4fc26" "basis" 1203 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{x-3})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(4)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{8}{4-3}+C \\\\ 1 & =-8+C \\\\ C & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "33d31df5c002d4c09c8da6a49f2643388148a2099bf31895c57ea2ce62f4fc26" "basis" 1203 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5577438eadf86b79813dc03e2fd7e3c8cd6ef835ab14f35430977dbeeac7846d" "basis" 1203 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "33d31df5c002d4c09c8da6a49f2643388148a2099bf31895c57ea2ce62f4fc26" "basis" 1203 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9-\\frac{8}{x-3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "33d31df5c002d4c09c8da6a49f2643388148a2099bf31895c57ea2ce62f4fc26" "basis" 1203 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+3{e}^{-x}=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-{e}^{-x})+C \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=-{e}^{-x/3}+C"] ["math" "f(x)=3{e}^{-x}+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}+C"] ["math" "f(x)={e}^{-3x}+C"] ["math" "f(x)={e}^{x-3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=3{e}^{-x}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{2x}=-2x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}-2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-4{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{2x}-2{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+6{x}^{2}=4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4x-6{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(3-x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)+C"] ["math" "f(x)={x}^{2}(2-x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)={x}^{2}(2x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $-5{f}^{′}(x)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\int \\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int \\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-99006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{9}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=20{x}^{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =20\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+C \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+Cx+D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=4{x}^{4}+C{x}^{2}+Dx"] ["math" "y=4{x}^{5}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=5{x}^{4}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y={x}^{5}+C{x}^{2}+Dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5=6{x}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-5x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-5x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=3{x}^{4}-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-4{x}^{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}+Cx+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=4x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-99009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y={x}^{3}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C+D"] ["math" "y={x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-99009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6x=8{e}^{x/2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{x/2}-6x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8{e}^{x/2}-6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(2{e}^{x/2})-6(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})+C \\\\  & =16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =16\\int {e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =16(2{e}^{x/2})-3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+Cx+D \\\\  & =32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119042" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=16{e}^{x/2}+{x}^{3}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=16{e}^{x/2}-3{x}^{3}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=32{e}^{x/2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119042" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=32{e}^{x/2}-{x}^{3}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{-2x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\int {e}^{-2x}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+C \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{-2x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-4{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=-{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+Dx"] ["math" "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=2{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+D"] ["math" "y={e}^{-2x}+C{x}^{2}+Dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119038" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-3,0,3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/2d64c09661973b7ef840e783a88de85d5ca9cf3436fae7eaebef36aca98ae631.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-50198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/25e8c2c60a948d324dc7b836815e81a0321b1353dafded0c789d53b9c73d5edc.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/5e94f63a81cee566fea810265d8a37959617abaf5a8c50250c269fe44584405e.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/81cc65015383f5c4b749a716d15b991d5a14d50d79aa866de22b41de0d802e53.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/93c572ba14dadbcabaf218f2395d51465ceef24d1c7c4083025ea67bb36ed438.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/d29058f4c71941f04dd2d934f1896972f0eb41a179984ec5d3675265ee9da56c.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/d29058f4c71941f04dd2d934f1896972f0eb41a179984ec5d3675265ee9da56c.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/64b0962fbb38b2c64da68de01d1c6407174aa66f810b820ece7185866b7f8ff3.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99f