\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-4{e}^{-x/4}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=0,3,6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/a4b534bd33daabc94aa3c86935b1fd4c0be723fafbc418ed382716541a864293.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/7832a2110292cb364cf06c24eb51e9bb1ee42fe430ac8fcc381af047a09125e4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/8ede6d26a62570f4037ecc58c377e95389ab00dbee36b60c46e6fb2021e01cea.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/96359fe35288b866cbf9fd929e2515af04a4ec0dc565a4cd4af9d3a8fcd20f94.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/cece096a5b267821994e9b6d8142f0d7ea684bbe8e28da7cdb01b87a73f1db4c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2(x-1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-1)^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/92a2dbaa5726e6a1ab83fa879ad7b630b05e68a8e366db214b74d85269a849a9.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-50195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/0ab0b12088ac6816f7086e952e749ea6d4c9107cc6189ebb0efcafb904152ad0.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/1a0e6d6d025e2f8b79019036637efd78b89954d1b01b00037ece77df4c3844eb.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/5d686380cd025e83e38524918c5cfaf215726f0f0d05783b8f88fd5f281c091c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/65ae1770ff4084d5a89fdda0f552f2a92380ae948c2b0f1ef3d3bb5d20f32713.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/8bd666d1415f83ff8232e39963248ef0afe62f39e66d5f3416ae18316453faa3.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/0ab0b12088ac6816f7086e952e749ea6d4c9107cc6189ebb0efcafb904152ad0.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}(x+2)^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{2}(x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int (x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/2ef13d3c7516974afcb94986ee9198b61d263f0ef53c344c02a5a8eb849e2c38.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-79566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/108aed53018d6fd0737f2e7725a87554342e20067e5035ff87959fcda2885d73.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/1c0d59930937ca24873ee68b8234647e59d65d075aaa7b2409adf814c274e3dd.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/4da0b446c5fa2cbc1e7cd36b23be142487ecd2d7c83f55276b249a712e49d343.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/6c67b35b6dad5ac54d013f3ea3c20be662a09c3b793ee71f08baa45bcba4362c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/f55575ecf51ce707283ca5bf8e8020e7384ebe65348196e3aa0581697addf7c0.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-79566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/f55575ecf51ce707283ca5bf8e8020e7384ebe65348196e3aa0581697addf7c0.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+C \\\\ -1 & =-2(0)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1"] ["math" "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1"] ["math" "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3"] ["math" "f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3"] ["math" "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}+{e}^{-2x}=8x$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8x-{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8x-{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-(-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})+C \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(0)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =4(0)^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2(0)}}{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-119075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=2{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "y=2{x}^{2}-2{e}^{-2x}+3"] ["math" "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "y=8{x}^{2}+2{e}^{-2x}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-119075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(x-3)^{2}{y}^{′}=8$ that satisfies the condition $y(4)=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{x-3})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(4)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{8}{4-3}+C \\\\ 1 & =-8+C \\\\ C & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9-\\frac{8}{x-3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-2.$\n\n$$\n(1+2x){f}^{′}(x)-2=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{1+2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=(1+2x).$ Then $\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2\\cdot 0|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-50159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2"] ["math" "f(x)=2x-2"] ["math" "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-2"] ["math" "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-1"] ["math" "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-50159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$f(x)=\\,${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+C \\\\ 2 & =3(1)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0ce3625e0df62ca0ea55575ada38985c21728032260dd59bc792c2c2e96634f"} {"question" "q-352075" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "q-352075" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\cos(x)-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/state.json" "file_sha256" "139deb4396cf089b3973227a22860595f35e5976c8e1e04bcd48054e99fcf0c8"} {"question" "e-528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f'(x) - 3\\sin(2x) = 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-528.json" "file_sha256" "3a32590f00e2c420f013da8f3a4737a8b530181d2ef9d897f50ac11c68eb5370"} {"question" "e-528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 3\\sin{2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-528.json" "file_sha256" "3a32590f00e2c420f013da8f3a4737a8b530181d2ef9d897f50ac11c68eb5370"} {"question" "e-529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2} = x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-529.json" "file_sha256" "e0189347ff677cac5ac0cfa1cd65796536d6ac8e035e18481ce2442d9eb3e72f"} {"question" "e-529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}+Cx+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$ We cannot combine them, because $C$ is being multiplied by $x$ while $D$ is not." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-529.json" "file_sha256" "e0189347ff677cac5ac0cfa1cd65796536d6ac8e035e18481ce2442d9eb3e72f"} {"question" "e-530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation $y'  = 2x,$ and sketch the solution curves of this equation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-530.json" "file_sha256" "eb8f9bff76fd68742c6211b9891714481c2e875dd07c3e70869697f423ae49c7"} {"question" "e-530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-530.json" "file_sha256" "eb8f9bff76fd68742c6211b9891714481c2e875dd07c3e70869697f423ae49c7"} {"question" "e-531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$$\nf'(x) - \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2} = 0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-531.json" "file_sha256" "5a875f1ec40961e0f37948d29a9fef85d57f5517e1aa46a89e350d8254139301"} {"question" "e-531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x) = 3\\arctan{x} + C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0) = 2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C \\\\ 2 & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)+C \\\\ 2 & =0+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\arctan x + 2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/example-531.json" "file_sha256" "5a875f1ec40961e0f37948d29a9fef85d57f5517e1aa46a89e350d8254139301"}] "usage" {"e-528" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283110}] "q-119043" [] "e-531" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283371}] "e-529" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283217}] "q-119045" [] "q-50136" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283112} {"kind" "responses" "entity" 17592186283112}] "q-50195" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283258} {"kind" "responses" "entity" 17592186283258}] "q-119032" [] "e-530" [{"kind" "presentations" "entity" 17592186283256}] "q-352066" [] "q-119035" [] "q-79563" [] "q-119132" []} "basis" 1488 "retractions" [[17592186292759 :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/64b0962fbb38b2c64da68de01d1c6407174aa66f810b820ece7185866b7f8ff3.png)"] [17592186292742 :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-4{e}^{-x/4}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=0,3,6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/a4b534bd33daabc94aa3c86935b1fd4c0be723fafbc418ed382716541a864293.png)"] [17592186097222 :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2(x - 1)$?"] [17592186097222 :question/worked-solution "Integrating $y'=2(x-1)$ gives\n$$y=(x-1)^2+C.$$\nThe solution curves are upward-opening parabolas, all with symmetry axis $x=1$, differing only by vertical translation. Select the diagram showing this family; its vertices all have $x$-coordinate $1$."] [17592186096421 :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095672 17592186095673 17592186095674 17592186095675 17592186095676 17592186095690 17592186095691 17592186095692 17592186095693 1